{red|**Honestly assess how fully you and your spouse have left your families of origin.**

Have you established your spouse as your primary loyalty?}{red| Do you make decisions as a couple or with heavy parental involvement?}{red| Is your spouse ever caught between you and your parents?}{red| Are there ways you have not fully left?}{red| Are there ways your parents have not fully released you?}

Write your honest assessment for yourself and your perception of your spouse:

{red|**Reflect on what boundaries you need with extended family.**

Where do you feel your marriage is not adequately protected from extended family intrusion?}{red| What patterns cause repeated conflict?}{red| What do you need to change about how extended family relates to you?}{red| What boundaries have you been reluctant to set?}

Write the boundaries you believe are needed:

{red|**Reflect on how you navigate loyalty conflicts in your marriage.**

When your spouse and your family are at odds, how do you typically respond?}{red| Does your spouse feel confident of your first loyalty, or do they feel like they come second to your family?}{red| Are there situations where you have sided with your family against your spouse?}{red| Are there complaints from your spouse about your family that you have not adequately addressed?}

Write your honest reflection:

{red|**Reflect on your current relationship with your own parents.**

How would you describe the relationship?}{red| Are appropriate boundaries in place?}{red| Do your parents respect your adulthood and marriage?}{red| Is there tension between honoring your parents and protecting your marriage?}{red| What would a healthier relationship look like?}

Write your reflection on your relationship with your own parents:

{red|**Identify one way you will work to improve the relationship between your parents and your marriage.**

**Maybe you need to address a boundary issue with your parents directly.** Maybe you need to help your spouse understand your family better. Maybe you need to increase or decrease contact to find a healthier balance. Maybe you need to advocate for your spouse in a situation you have been avoiding.

What specific step will you take regarding your relationship with your own parents?}

{red|**Reflect on your relationships with your in-laws.**

How would you describe these relationships currently?}{red| What is going well?}{red| What is challenging?}{red| Are there ways you could invest more in these relationships?}{red| Are there boundaries you need that would actually help the relationship?}

Write your reflection on your in-law relationships:

{red|**Reflect on how you have navigated holidays in your marriage.**

What approaches have you used?}{red| What has worked well?}{red| What has created conflict?}{red| Does one family consistently get more time than the other?}{red| Has the pressure of holiday navigation created resentment between you and your spouse?}

Write about your holiday history and what needs to change:

{red|**If you have children, reflect on the grandparent relationships in your family.**

What is working well in these relationships?}{red| What challenges exist?}{red| Are there boundary issues that need to be addressed?}{red| Is there imbalance between the two sets of grandparents that needs attention?}

Write your reflection on grandparent dynamics in your family:

{red|**Reflect on any complicated extended family situations you navigate.**

What complexity exists in your or your spouse's family of origin?}{red| How have you handled it so far?}{red| What is working and what is not?}{red| Is there a situation where protective distance may be necessary?}{red| How can you better support each other in navigating family complexity?}

Write your reflection on complicated family situations:

{red|What is the most important thing you learned about navigating extended family through this journey?}

{red|What do you want to remember when extended family challenges arise?}{red| How has your understanding of these relationships changed?}

Write your greatest insight:

{red|Based on this journey, what specific changes will you make in how you navigate extended family relationships?}

**Consider boundaries you will establish, conversations you will have, approaches you will change, and ways you will support each other better.**

